  "rationale": "This is a significant Athenian honorific decree from the mid-2nd century BC. It documents the career of Miltiades of Marathon, highlighting the Hellenistic practice of liturgy and euergetism, where wealthy citizens funded essential city functions like grain supply and religious festivals (the Panathenaia) from their private wealth. The text also provides valuable topographical information regarding the Kerameikos and the repair of public monuments such as the Anakeion and the Long Stoa.",
